    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38931" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Prŏpontis</span></b>  (Prōpontis,
				<i><span class="en">Manil. 4, 676</span></i>), ĭdos
		and ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Προποντίς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the Propontis</i> or <i>Sea
				of Marmora</i>, <i>between the Hellespont and the
				Thracian Bosporus</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 1, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 3, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12,
				24, § 76</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 38,
			16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 2, 54</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 3,
			6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cat. 4, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. P. 4,
				9, 118</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Prŏpontĭăcus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Propontis</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aqua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				3</span></i>
			 (4), 21, 1: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 1, 10, 29</span></i>
			.</div>
